@model string
<section id="file-tools">
    <h2>File tools</h2>
    <p>Choose the input and a new output file using native dialogs. Existing files are never overwritten.</p>
    <p>Base64 is encoding, not encryption. MD5 and SHA-1 are provided for legacy checksums, not security verification.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/FileTools" hx-post="/FileTools" hx-target="#file-tools" hx-swap="outerHTML">
        @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
        <label>Operation <select name="Operation">
            <option value="Sha256">SHA-256</option>
            <option value="Sha384">SHA-384</option>
            <option value="Sha512">SHA-512</option>
            <option value="Md5">MD5 (legacy)</option>
            <option value="Sha1">SHA-1 (legacy)</option>
            <option value="Base64Encode">Base64 encode</option>
            <option value="Base64Decode">Base64 decode</option>
        </select></label>
        <button>Choose files and run</button>
    </form>
    <h3>Detached CMS signature verification</h3>
    <p>Select the original data file, then its `.p7c` signature. Validity and system certificate-chain trust are reported separately. This does not establish a trusted identity, timestamp or revocation status.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/FileTools?handler=VerifySignature" hx-post="/FileTools?handler=VerifySignature" hx-target="#file-tools" hx-swap="outerHTML">
        @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
        <button>Choose data and CMS signature to verify</button>
    </form>
    <h3>Portable password file encryption</h3>
    <p>Uses the compatible TM/jnUtil file format on Windows, Linux and macOS. Source files are retained: encryption does not delete or secure the original plaintext. Output files must be new, and losing the password prevents decryption.</p>
    <p>Legacy encryption cannot be interrupted mid-call. Cancellation prevents publishing its output after the call finishes. Deleted temporary files are not securely erased.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/FileTools?handler=Password" hx-post="/FileTools?handler=Password" hx-target="#file-tools" hx-swap="outerHTML">
        @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
        <label>Password operation <select name="PasswordOperation">
            <option value="Encrypt">Encrypt with password</option>
            <option value="Decrypt">Decrypt with password</option>
        </select></label>
        <label>File password <input type="password" name="FilePassword" required maxlength="4096" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        <label>Confirm file password (encryption only) <input type="password" name="ConfirmFilePassword" maxlength="4096" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        <button>Choose files and encrypt/decrypt</button>
    </form>
    <p role="status">@Model</p>
</section>
